🚨 After-hours Watch｜Hormuz sounds the alarm again—will BTC hold at $75,000 or surge to liquidate $8 billion of short positions?

📌 Close of day: 3 things
1) Iran attacked a U.S. military base in Kuwait. Trump changed his tone to “soon it will be over,” but has already ordered that “at any moment we can strike again.” Only 6 ships passed through the Strait of Hormuz yesterday;
2) Forbes: Rumors that Fed Chair Warsh may take office are gaining traction. BTC traders are positioning for a softer outlook toward $75,000;
3) On-chain data: Under key levels for BTC and ETH, roughly $8 billion worth of short orders have piled up—if price spikes upward, it could trigger a chain of liquidations.

💡 Digital signals
- Oil: Asia LNG hits a three-year high; U.S. diesel reaches a new high since April; Europe forward electricity prices keep climbing;
- Bonds: WSJ says “energy is pushing U.S. Treasury yields” has become the new main theme;
- On-chain: Binance’s featured area has a reminder: “Nearly $8 billion in short positions is hanging over the heads of BTC/ETH.”

🔥 Flows
- 21 banks (including Goldman Sachs, Bank of America, Citigroup, Morgan, Wells Fargo, Deutsche Bank, UBS, Fidelity, WisdomTree, etc.) announced they will set up companies in the second half of 2026 and issue dollar stablecoins in the first half of 2027—first in compliance with the GENIUS Act;
- But Circle’s stock fell about 6% that day; the market treats it as a potential competitor to existing dollar stablecoins (USDT supply: $180 billion);
- StarkWare completed “soft-fork-free quantum resistance” BTC mainnet transactions, adding ammunition to the long-term narrative.

📈 Evening market outlook
- Short term: Energy + rates + a strong dollar are still weighing on BTC. The real support below is the $75,000 psychological level;
- Medium term: 21 banks’ stablecoin moves + the CLARITY Act Senate vote on 9/15 = the door to fiat compliance opens—actually a structural long-positive;
- Risk: If Hormuz passage volume stays below the daily average for long, a stagflation shock could crush all risk assets.

❓ Interactive question
On the evening flows, which side are you on?
A. Hold $75,000, wait and see
B. The $8 billion shorts liquidation is imminent—bet on a wick
C. Buy as it drops—2026 bank stablecoins are a big positive
D. Don’t touch it; wait for clarity after the 9/15 CLARITY vote

